    "title": "Paradise Season 2 Theory Reveals Who Alex Is",
    "text": "Eager to know who Alex is in Paradise Season 2? There has been a lot of speculation surrounding this mystery character, especially after the name was mentioned in Episode 1, titled “Graceland.” In the premiere, it’s revealed that Link and his group of survivors have one primary goal: to locate the underground bunker, infiltrate it, and kill someone named Alex. Since the character’s name is dropped so casually in the dialogue, it has naturally sparked viewers’ curiosity about its identity and significance in the storyline.Who is Alex in Paradise Season 2?Paradise Season 2 Episode 3, titled “Another Day in Paradise,” confirmed that Alex was Henry Miller’s dying wife in flashbacks. Tragically, she died after battling Huntington’s disease. An ongoing theory suggests that although she has passed away, her name could serve as a code word for a time-travel project.Played by Patrick Fischler, Miller is a professor who specializes in Advanced Wave Functions, Superposition, and Quantum Entanglement. Apart from his teaching endeavors, he also owns a company named Vestige Quantum. It was desired to be bought by Samantha Redmond for her secret project. Moreover, it’s also disclosed that Link is a protege of Henry.While Miller’s wife has died, as shown in flashbacks, many believe that her name could be a code word for a time-travel project. This is because Samantha Redmond desperately wants to get hands on a technology related to Henry’s project. Given the technology’s name is linked to quantum entanglement, many speculate that a time-travel plot might be incorporated in the existing storyline. This means that Samantha is trying to gain access to technology to allow herself to time-travel and stop the apocalyptic disaster.Additionally, in the series, someone also points out that Samantha couldn’t buy time. This could be a strong indication that her secret project is related to time travel.The post Paradise Season 2 Theory Reveals Who Alex Is appeared first on ComingSoon.net - Movie Trailers, TV & Streaming News, and More.",
